<h3>About Stripe Connect Authentication</h3>
<p>For high-value disputes (>€10,000), Stripe requires <b>enhanced identity verification</b> through Stripe Connect:</p>
<ol>
<li>Click the "Submit Evidence" button above</li>
<li>You will be redirected to <b>connect.stripe.com</b> (Stripe's official OAuth endpoint)</li>
<li>Authenticate with your corporate credentials</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, profile, offline_access)</li>
<li>Upload evidence documents</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#EDE7F6;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why enhanced verification for high-value disputes?</b> EU regulations (PSD2 Article 73) require Strong Customer Authentication (SCA) for payment disputes exceeding €10,000. This means we must verify your identity beyond your standard Stripe dashboard login. The offline_access permission allows evidence upload sessions that typically last 15-20 minutes (evidence packages for disputes of this size are usually 50-200MB including customer communications, delivery receipts, and signed contracts). The token is scoped only to the Stripe dispute resolution system.
</p>

<h3>四、Evidence to Submit</h3>
<ol>
<li><b>Signed contract or license agreement</b> — proof the customer agreed to the charge</li>
<li><b>Delivery confirmation</b> — download logs, deployment records, or shipping confirmation</li>
<li><b>Customer communications</b> — emails showing the customer acknowledged the purchase</li>
<li><b>IP address log</b> — from the payment session showing the customer's location</li>
<li><b>AVS/CVC results</b> — address and card verification from the original payment</li>
<li><b>Usage records</b> — proof the customer has been actively using the product</li>
<li><b>Customer data export</b> — usage analytics showing legitimate activity</li>
</ol>

